AVM: build UTM's Metal SPICE display only when QEMU has OpenGL

ui/spice-display-metal.m (added by UTM) includes ui/egl-helpers.h, which
needs libepoxy, and uses ANGLE's Metal device from egl-helpers.c. Every
call into it is under HAVE_SPICE_GL, which exists only with CONFIG_OPENGL,
so without OpenGL nothing can use it. UTM's ui/meson.build compiles it
whenever Metal is available, so a build without the GPU stack (as
Tools/build-sysroot.sh makes for AVM, whose guest display is plain
virtio-gpu-pci) fails on 'epoxy/gl.h' file not found. This makes the
file need OpenGL too. Builds with OpenGL are unchanged.

Applied after UTM's own patches/qemu-10.0.12-utm.patch.

--- a/ui/meson.build	2026-10-25 21:57:13
+++ b/ui/meson.build	2026-10-25 21:57:13
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@
   if quartzcore.found()
     spice_core_ss.add(quartzcore)
   endif
-  if metal.found()
+  if metal.found() and opengl.found()
     spice_core_ss.add(metal)
     spice_core_ss.add(files('spice-display-metal.m'))
   endif
